BT 1 0 0 1 0 91.4 Tm -0.007971 Tw 12.6 TL /F1 9.4 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Cleaning guarantees that data is ) Tj /F5 9.4 Tf (well-formed) Tj /F1 9.4 Tf (, not that it is ) Tj /F5 9.4 Tf (true) Tj /F1 9.4 Tf (. Examples from our data: \(1\) 192.168.56.20:3306 had a) Tj T* 0 Tw (blank state; the services table shows MySQL 5.0.51a \(a High-severity finding\), but the cleaner cannot know whether) Tj T* (the port was open, so it stays in review and is missing from the master table until an analyst rescans - an automatic) Tj T* -0.090667 Tw (pass would either drop a real exposure or invent one. \(2\) 192.168.56.20:22 was recorded both open and filtered; only a) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.116393 Tw (new observation can decide. \(3\) The lookup maps freeciv to adb: a wrong lookup entry would be applied consistently to) Tj T* 0 Tw (every record, producing confidently wrong output. \(4\) A 'closed' or 'filtered' state may be caused by a firewall, rate) Tj T* (limiting or timing, so format-correct data can still be a false negative. Therefore human review, rescanning and source) Tj T* (verification remain necessary.) Tj T* ET
